&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.greenhouse.com/mission&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;mission&lt;/a&gt; at Greenhouse is to make hiring work for everyone – so we go to great lengths to hire great people because we believe that they’re the foundation of our success. At Greenhouse, you’ll join a team that collaborates purposefully, fosters inclusivity, and communicates with transparency and accountability so we can achieve our mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us to do the best work of your career, solving meaningful problems with remarkable teams.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Greenhouse is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Director, People Systems &amp;amp; Operations&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;to join our team!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to our Chief People Officer and sitting on the People Leadership Team (PLT), you will serve as the strategic and operational leader for our People Operations and People Systems function. You will drive data integrity, compliance, technology enablement, and operational excellence across the entire employee lifecycle, from onboarding through offboarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a champion of continuous process improvement, scalable automation, and you will operationalize Greenhouse&#39;s AI-forward approach to how we run our own People function. You will partner closely with COEs — the teams who own hiring, development, rewards, and belonging — to unlock one continuous and coherent employee experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who will love this job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An innovative builder – &lt;/strong&gt;you are energized by new technology and exploring ways to elevate existing processes with new tools, you thrive when designing seamless and elegant employee processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A systems thinker – &lt;/strong&gt;you are passionate about HR tech, process automation, and analytics, and see AI as a tool for removing friction, not adding it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A data-driven decision maker –&lt;/strong&gt; you leverage metrics to drive continuous improvement and help leaders retain their best people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An influential champion — &lt;/strong&gt;You effectively manage relationships across all levels and functions. You drive clarity, empower others and enable business outcomes to support Greenhouse in its next stage of growth. A cross-functional collaborator – you build trust and engagement across teams without needing to own every piece of the outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A change architect – &lt;/strong&gt;you are energized by leading through systems upgrades, AI adoption, policy refreshes, and new ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A growth mindset evangelist —&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;You cultivate winning teams that thrive by unlocking potential and instilling a culture of continuous up-skilling, within your team and throughout the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the strategy and roadmap for Greenhouse’s HR technology ecosystem from implementation, configuration, integrations, user experience, continuous improvement, and vendor relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the HRIS as the single source of truth for employee data. Drive automation, data accuracy, governance, stakeholder adoption, and reliable downstream connections to payroll, benefits, analytics, and other People systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use the employee journey to improve the moments that matter—from offer and onboarding through promotions, leaves of absence, and offboarding. Partner with program owners across People to make candidate, manager, and employee experiences more connected and effective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable people analytics, dashboards, and self-service tools that give leaders the insight to make better workforce decisions, address retention risks early, and improve information flow to employees and managers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own People-related compliance across the employee lifecycle (immigration, leaves of absence, audits, and evolving labor requirements) as Greenhouse grows globally. Serve as the escalation point for complex policy questions, compliance issues, and high-priority employee matters, partnering with Legal as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Greenhouse’s AI-forward evolution within People processes and operations. Apply our AI Principles Framework to People Operations, pilot Greenhouse AI capabilities in our own workflows, and translate learnings into structured feedback for Product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion experimentation and continuous improvement by testing new tools, processes, and workflows in contained ways before scaling them. Partner across IT, Finance, Legal, Talent Acquisition &amp;amp; Planning, Talent Management/Org Development, Total Rewards, and IDEA to align People Operations with company priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute the People Operations perspective to company-wide People strategy as a member of the People Leadership Team, while developing and empowering a high-performing team through clear priorities, coaching, performance management, and growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional projects and responsibilities as business needs require&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You should have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of progressive People Operations experience, including 3+ years leading People Operations, HRIS, and/or People Systems teams at the manager or director level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience administering and optimizing relevant, global HRIS platforms (Workday, Rippling, HiBob, etc) including implementations, integrations, automation, data integrity, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of designing and scaling People processes that improve efficiency, data quality, compliance, or employee experience, with measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payroll and benefits integrations, cross-border employee data and reporting requirements, and workforce data privacy; global experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience evaluating, piloting, or implementing AI and automation in a People operations context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management, change leadership, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to create structure and momentum in a fast-paced, dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An analytical, data-driven approach and proficiency with HR reporting, dashboarding, and self-service tools — paired with the ability to turn workforce data into clear recommendations for leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and leading high-performing, diverse teams, and the ability to operate as a strategic partner at the leadership-team level while staying close enough to the details of a workflow, system, or dataset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your own unique talents! Your background has given you a unique perspective and set of transferable skills that aren&#39;t always in alignment with a given role - but those are qualities we value at Greenhouse. If you don&#39;t meet 100% of the qualifications outlined above, we still strongly encourage you to apply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you are based in California, we encourage you to read this important information for California residents linked&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.greenhouse.io/ccpa-candidate&quot;&gt; &lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The national pay range for this role is $153,300–$185,400. Individual compensation will be commensurate with the candidate&#39;s experience and qualifications. Certain roles may be eligible for additional compensation, including stock option awards, bonuses, and merit increases. Additionally, certain roles have the opportunity to receive sales commissions that are based on the terms of the sales commission plan applicable to the role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Greenhouse provides a variety of benefits to employees, including medical, dental, and vision insurance, basic life insurance, mental health resources, financial wellness benefits, and a fully paid parental leave program. For US-based employees, we offer short-term and long-term disability coverage, a 401(k) plan and company match. U.S. based employees also receive, per calendar year, up to 14 scheduled paid holidays and up to 80 hours of paid sick leave. Non-exempt employees accrue up to 20-25 days of paid vacation time annually, depending on tenure, and exempt employees have flexible paid time off (PTO).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The anticipated closing date for this role is September 28, 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Greenhouse, we live by our mission through &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.greenhouse.com/interviewing-at-greenhouse&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;using our own product&lt;/a&gt; to help us hire the right person for the job, every time. We’re committed to designing and responsibly using AI tools to transform how we work while keeping people at the center. We are a remote-first company and have shared office spaces in New York City and Ireland, and optional co-working spaces that give us flexibility to do our best work anywhere. We take an active role in our growth through a performance review program that’s committed to providing actionable feedback, and a bonus structure that rewards great performance. We believe that bringing together a variety of perspectives makes us a stronger company – and we nurture leaders who create an inclusive culture and invest into employee resource groups that celebrate our differences and life experiences. We’re proud to have built an&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.greenhouse.com/awards&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;award-winning culture&lt;/a&gt; that’s been recognized as Fortune’s Best Places to Work and Inc.’s Best Workplaces multiple years in a row.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;–&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Greenhouse Software is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, or gender identity), national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable local laws, regulations and ordinances. If you need assistance and/or a reasonable accommodation during the application process, reach out to accommodations@greenhouse.io.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Emails about job opportunities at Greenhouse Software are only offered by employees with @greenhouse.io email addresses. See &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.greenhouse.com/candidate-phishing-scams&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;this page&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; on our website if you suspect a phishing scam.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.greenhouse.com/mission&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;mission&lt;/a&gt; at Greenhouse is to make hiring work for everyone – so we go to great lengths to hire great people because we believe that they’re the foundation of our success. At Greenhouse, you’ll join a team that collaborates purposefully, fosters inclusivity, and communicates with transparency and accountability so we can achieve our mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us to do the best work of your career, solving meaningful problems with remarkable teams.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Greenhouse is looking for an Engineering Manager to join our team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits on our Cloud Platform team. Reporting to the Director of Platform Engineering, this people management role will lead engineers responsible for core AWS cloud foundations and our Kubernetes platform, helping ensure our infrastructure is scalable, secure, resilient, and cost-effective for internal engineering teams and our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Engineering Manager, you’ll set technical priorities across cloud infrastructure, reliability, security, and cost management while creating the conditions for your team to do their best work. You’ll partner closely with Security and the broader Platform leadership group on shared standards, roadmaps, incident response, and cross-team priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who will love this job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;leader&lt;/strong&gt; – you enjoy coaching and developing engineers while building a strong, accountable, and healthy team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;platform-builder&lt;/strong&gt; – you’re motivated by creating scalable, secure, and reliable infrastructure that other engineering teams depend on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;technical operator&lt;/strong&gt; – you’re comfortable owning production systems, managing incidents, and improving reliability over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;prioritizer&lt;/strong&gt; – you know how to balance reliability, security, cost, and delivery against company and department goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;collaborator&lt;/strong&gt; – you work effectively across platform, security, finance, and leadership to move shared priorities forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;problem-solver&lt;/strong&gt; – you like digging into complex cloud and Kubernetes challenges and turning them into durable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of engineers; manage performance and create the conditions for them to do their best work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own AWS cloud foundations across compute, networking, identity, and core services, serving as the team’s technical owner and primary escalation point&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cloud cost observability and attribution by establishing and refining tagging, reporting, and accountability practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend and execute commitment-based AWS cost strategies, including evaluating and managing Savings Plans and Reserved Instances based on usage forecasts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and communicate technical priorities for the team, balancing reliability, security, cost, and delivery against department and company objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the platform remains scalable, secure, and resilient and continues to meet the needs of internal engineering teams and our customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Security team and the broader Platform management group on shared standards, infrastructure roadmaps, incident response, and cross-team priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience working within a cloud platform or infrastructure-focused organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of technical prioritization and managing Kubernetes at scale in production, including cluster lifecycle and upgrades&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong, hands-on familiarity with the AWS ecosystem, including compute, networking, IAM/identity, and core services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading, coaching, or managing engineers through formal people management or significant tech lead responsibility, with a record of growing and retaining talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with infrastructure as code and GitOps practices such as Terraform and Helm, and managing change across shared infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication skills with the ability to align technical priorities to department and company objectives and partner across security, engineering, and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your own unique talents! Your background has given you a unique perspective and set of transferable skills that aren&#39;t always in alignment with a given role - but those are qualities we value at Greenhouse. If you don&#39;t meet 100% of the qualifications outlined above, we still strongly encourage you to apply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Applicants must be legally eligible to work in Canada as of the start date chosen by the Company.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;For purposes of processing or administering your employment relationship, personal information that you provide to the Company may be transferred to and accessed by an affiliate in the United States or elsewhere, or to agents and contractors (such as payroll companies, insurance companies, information technology consultants, etc.) that provide services to the Company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The national pay range for this role is $129,000 - $175,000 CAD. Individual compensation will be commensurate with the candidate&#39;s experience and qualifications. Certain roles may be eligible for additional compensation, including stock option awards, bonuses, and merit increases. Additionally, certain roles have the opportunity to receive sales commissions that are based on the terms of the sales commission plan applicable to the role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
